    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.is_maximal_matching - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.is_maximal_matching.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.is_maximal_matching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if a set of edges is a maximal matching.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.is_maximal_matching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if a set of edges is a maximal matching.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.is_maximal_matching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Check if a set of edges is a maximal matching.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCheck if a set of edges is a maximal matching.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L83288-L83385){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.is_maximal_matching(edges)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Is maximal matching](../assets/graphs/is-maximal-matching.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The path A-B-C-D on both sides, with the candidate edges drawn as the input. Left: the middle edge B-C alone; both other edges touch B or C, so nothing can be added and is_maximal_matching() returns True. Right: A-B alone; the edge C-D (shown in the accent color with its free endpoints C and D) could still be added, so is_maximal_matching() returns False.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nA matching is a set of edges with no shared endpoints. It is *maximal* when no other\nedge of the graph can be added without breaking that rule: every edge has at least one\nendpoint that is already matched. Maximal is weaker than maximum (largest possible):\n`maximal_matching()` returns maximal matchings quickly, while `maximum_weight_matching()`\non an unweighted graph returns a maximum one, and every maximum matching is maximal.\n\nEdge direction is ignored. Self-loops cannot be part of a matching, and they are not\nneeded to make it maximal.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[edges]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [list[int]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A list of integer edge IDs, such as the output of `maximal_matching()`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   `True` if the edges exist, form a matching, and no edge can be added to it.\n    Unknown edge IDs give `False`.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nThe check marks the matched nodes and then makes one pass over the edges, looking\nfor a non-loop edge whose two endpoints are both unmatched. It runs in $O(V + E)$.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~is_matching`) \n\n:   Check that no two edges share a node.\n\n[](`~maximal_matching`) \n\n:   Find a maximal matching quickly.\n\n[](`~bipartite_maximum_matching`) \n\n:   The largest matching of a bipartite graph.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nIn the path `A`-`B`-`C`-`D`, the middle edge alone is maximal, since both outer edges\ntouch `B` or `C`. It isn't the largest, though: the two outer edges make a matching of\ntwo. The edge `A`-`B` alone isn't maximal, since `C`-`D` can be added:\n\n::: {#8c71742f .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\npath = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\nab, bc, cd = (\n    path.find_edge_ids(u, v)[0]\n    for u, v in [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")]\n)\n\n(\n    path.is_maximal_matching([bc]),\n    path.is_maximal_matching([ab, cd]),\n    path.is_maximal_matching([ab]),\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(True, True, False)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### A plan that can't grow but isn't the best\n\n`teams()` links the 8 workers of a made-up software team to the 8 tasks of a release that\neach can do. Giving Omar the Backend task and Kofi the Database task leaves DevOps and\nSecurity with no one free to take them, and Hana and Luis with nothing left that they can\ndo. The plan is maximal, with six tasks covered, but seven is possible:\n\n::: {#0feefca2 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nteam = ec.teams()\nplan = {\n    \"Omar\": \"Backend\", \"Priya\": \"Testing\", \"Tom\": \"Frontend\",\n    \"Mei\": \"Design\", \"Sara\": \"Docs\", \"Kofi\": \"Database\",\n}\nmatched = [team.find_edge_ids(w, t)[0] for w, t in plan.items()]\n\n(\n    team.is_maximal_matching(matched),\n    len(matched),\n    len(team.bipartite_maximum_matching()),\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(True, 6, 7)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#7bba6c62 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nteam.layout_bipartite(align=\"horizontal\", aspect_ratio=0.4).plot(\n    layout=\"pos\",\n    highlight={\"soft\": [\"Hana\", \"Luis\", \"DevOps\", \"Security\"]},\n    highlight_edges=matched,\n    label_by=\"label\",\n    height=300,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-9f8a22df:#efc5b7;--ect-6c2f7015:#a78980;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-9f8a22df:#4c2e23;--ect-6c2f7015:#352018;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-9f8a22df:#efc5b7;--ect-6c2f7015:#a78980;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-9f8a22df:#4c2e23;--ect-6c2f7015:#352018;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"300\" viewBox=\"11.1 14.0 681.3 292.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacS